{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CesegCwL7L24qDHHopXGu","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on my exploration, here is my analysis:\n\n**Requirement, restated:**\nAdd `POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel` endpoint that cancels active orders (moving them to `CANCELLED` status), handles idempotent retries, prevents cancellation when shipments are confirmed, and prevents shipment creation for cancelled orders.\n\n**Repository findings:**\n- `Order.kt` (line 11-16): Order data class lacks status field\n- `OrderController.kt` (line 15-46): Has create, getById, list; needs cancel endpoint\n- `OrderRepository.kt` (line 10-27): InMemoryOrderRepository for persistence\n- `Shipment.kt` (line 9-27): Already has `ShipmentStatus` enum with CREATED, CONFIRMED, CANCELLED\n- `ShipmentController.kt` (line 21-56): Create, getById, list; needs order status validation\n- `ShipmentRepository.kt` (line 10-27): InMemoryShipmentRepository; needs method to find by orderId\n- `ApiExceptions.kt` (line 11-31): Exception hierarchy (ResourceNotFoundException→404, ConflictException→409)\n- `ApiError.kt` (line 31-37): ErrorCode enum with existing codes\n- `GlobalExceptionHandler.kt` (line 14-29): Wraps exceptions in ApiError envelope\n\n**Conventions already in place:**\n1. API failures throw ApiException subclasses with status code and ErrorCode\n2. Error responses follow ApiError envelope with code, message, fields\n3. Domain errors use specific ErrorCode values (ORDER_ALREADY_EXISTS, SHIPMENT_ALREADY_EXISTS)\n4. In-memory repositories use ConcurrentHashMap\n5. Tests verify both HTTP status and error envelope structure\n6. Create endpoints use separate Request DTOs\n\n**Affected files:**\n1. `Order.kt` - Add OrderStatus enum and status field (cannot avoid, core domain change)\n2. `OrderController.kt` - Add cancel endpoint (required by ticket)\n3. `ShipmentRepository.kt` - Add findByOrderId() method (required to find shipments to cancel)\n4. `ShipmentController.kt` - Validate order not cancelled when creating (required by ticket)\n5. `ApiError.kt` - Add error codes for order cancellation scenarios (required for error consistency)\n6. `OrderControllerTest.kt` - Add tests for cancel scenarios (required by acceptance criteria #5)\n\n**Risks:**\n1. Idempotence of cancel on already-cancelled order must succeed without error\n2. All-or-nothing atomicity: if one shipment cancel fails, order must remain ACTIVE\n3. Concurrent cancellations of same order from multiple threads\n4. Existing tests may expect Order to not have status field\n\n**Open questions:**\nNone - the ticket is clear about required behavior and follows established patterns.\n\n---\n\n```\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n```\n\n**Proposed change, file by file:**\n\n1. **Order.kt** - Add `OrderStatus` enum (ACTIVE, CANCELLED) and `status: OrderStatus` field to Order. Update CreateOrderRequest to match.\n\n2. **OrderController.kt** - Add `POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel` endpoint that:\n   - Returns 404 if order not found (OrderRepository.findById → throw ResourceNotFoundException)\n   - Returns 409 if any shipment is CONFIRMED (throw ConflictException with ORDER_HAS_CONFIRMED_SHIPMENT)\n   - Succeeds idempotently if order is already CANCELLED\n   - Sets order status to CANCELLED and cancels all CREATED shipments if ACTIVE\n   - Returns updated order with 200 OK\n\n3. **ShipmentRepository.kt** - Add `findByOrderId(orderId: String): List<Shipment>` to support the cancel operation.\n\n4. **ShipmentController.kt** - In create endpoint, add validation: if order exists and is CANCELLED, throw ConflictException with ORDER_IS_CANCELLED. If order doesn't exist, allow shipment creation (preserve existing behavior per ticket).\n\n5. **ApiError.kt** - Add two error codes: `ORDER_HAS_CONFIRMED_SHIPMENT` (when shipment blocks cancel), `ORDER_IS_CANCELLED` (when shipment rejected for cancelled order).\n\n6. **OrderControllerTest.kt** - Add tests covering:\n   - Cancel active order: status changes to CANCELLED, shipments in CREATED status are cancelled\n   - Cancel already-cancelled order: succeeds, returns cancelled order, changes nothing\n   - Cancel with confirmed shipment: 409 ConflictException, order stays ACTIVE, all shipments unchanged\n   - Cancel non-existent order: 404 ResourceNotFoundException\n   - Verify error envelope structure\n\n7. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt** - Add test that creating shipment for CANCELLED order returns 409 with ORDER_IS_CANCELLED error code.\n\n**Alternative considered and rejected:**\n- *Alternative: Make cancel idempotent at the repository level, having it return boolean (cancelled vs already cancelled).* Rejected because the endpoint must return the order entity, and the pattern in this codebase is for controllers to throw exceptions for error cases, not for repositories to return status flags. Idempotence is better handled by checking order status before throwing.\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n\n*Case 1: Cancel ACTIVE order successfully*\n- Controller receives POST /orders/O-1/cancel\n- Controller calls repository.findById(\"O-1\") → Order(status=ACTIVE)\n- Controller calls shipmentRepository.findByOrderId(\"O-1\") → [S-1(status=CREATED), S-2(status=CONFIRMED)]\n- Throws ConflictException(\"ORDER_HAS_CONFIRMED_SHIPMENT\") → 409 response, nothing changes\n\nWait, let me re-read the case. If CONFIRMED exists, we reject. Let me trace the success case:\n\n*Case 1: Cancel ACTIVE order with only CREATED shipments*\n- POST /orders/O-1/cancel\n- findById(\"O-1\") → Order(status=ACTIVE)\n- findByOrderId(\"O-1\") → [S-1(status=CREATED), S-2(status=CREATED)]\n- For each shipment: update status to CANCELLED, save to repository\n- Update order status to CANCELLED, save to repository\n- Return updated order with 200 OK\n\n*Case 2: Cancel already-CANCELLED order*\n- POST /orders/O-1/cancel\n- findById(\"O-1\") → Order(status=CANCELLED)\n- Return order with 200 OK (no changes, idempotent)\n\n*Case 3: Cancel ACTIVE order with CONFIRMED shipment*\n- POST /orders/O-1/cancel\n- findById(\"O-1\") → Order(status=ACTIVE)\n- findByOrderId(\"O-1\") → [S-1(status=CONFIRMED)]\n- Throw ConflictException(\"ORDER_HAS_CONFIRMED_SHIPMENT\", \"Order has confirmed shipment\")\n- 409 response, nothing modified\n\n*Case 4: Cancel non-existent order*\n- POST /orders/O-missing/cancel\n- findById(\"O-missing\") → null\n- Throw ResourceNotFoundException(\"ORDER_NOT_FOUND\", \"No order with id 'O-missing'\")\n- 404 response\n\n*Case 5: Create shipment for CANCELLED order*\n- POST /shipments with orderId=O-cancelled\n- orderRepository.findById(\"O-cancelled\") → Order(status=CANCELLED)\n- Throw ConflictException(\"ORDER_IS_CANCELLED\", \"Order is cancelled\")\n- 409 response\n\n*Case 6: Create shipment for non-existent order*\n- POST /shipments with orderId=O-missing\n- orderRepository.findById(\"O-missing\") → null\n- Proceed with shipment creation (current behavior preserved)\n\n**Test strategy:**\n\nOrderControllerTest additions:\n1. `cancel_active_order_succeeds` - Create order O-1, create shipments S-1(CREATED), S-2(CREATED), POST cancel, verify order status=CANCELLED, verify S-1 and S-2 status=CANCELLED\n2. `cancel_active_order_with_confirmed_shipment_rejects` - Create order, create shipment S-1(CONFIRMED), POST cancel, verify 409 ConflictException with ORDER_HAS_CONFIRMED_SHIPMENT, verify order still ACTIVE, verify shipment still CONFIRMED\n3. `cancel_already_cancelled_order_succeeds_idempotently` - Create order, cancel it, cancel again, verify 200 OK both times, verify order unchanged\n4. `cancel_nonexistent_order_returns_404` - POST cancel for non-existent order, verify 404 ResourceNotFoundException with ORDER_NOT_FOUND\n5. `cancel_returns_updated_order_json` - Verify JSON response includes status field\n\nShipmentControllerTest additions:\n1. `create_shipment_for_cancelled_order_rejects` - Create order, cancel it, try to create shipment, verify 409 ConflictException with ORDER_IS_CANCELLED\n2. `create_shipment_for_nonexistent_order_succeeds` - Try to create shipment with non-existent orderId, verify succeeds (current behavior)\n\n---\n\n```\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>\n```\n\nNow I'll implement the changes. Starting with Order.kt to add the status field:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2058,"cache_read_input_tokens":19272,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2058},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"af144e0f-ba7a-4bf1-85ab-b9c7bd0372da","uuid":"6fcfcc26-4b19-4661-be8b-e489068c55b3","timestamp":"2026-09-09T09:45:19.233Z","request_id":"req_011CesegCJtByjUeG4HS9bcd"}
